<figure class="restore" data-r19-restore aria-labelledby="r19-restore-title">
 <figcaption id="r19-restore-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A clean database can still be missing a valid order</figcaption>
 <div class="history"><div><b>Saved base</b><span>103 present</span></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Target</b><span>Before mistake</span></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Bad transaction</b><span>Deletes 103</span></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Valid later work</b><span>107 + one P3</span></div></div>
 <div class="states"><div><b>Old source authority</b><p data-source data-live>Open · still accepting requests</p></div><div><b>Candidate database</b><p data-candidate data-live>Not restored</p></div><div><b>Acceptance</b><p data-accept data-live>No authority transfer</p></div></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The bad transaction removed order 103. Valid order 107 then took P3 stock from 10 to 9.</p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Restore and reconciliation steps"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>The complete recovery sequence</summary><ol><li>Bad deletion removes 103; valid 107 consumes one P3.</li><li>Fence the old source; resolve admitted work and reject the boundary race. Freeze its accepted history.</li><li>Restore the saved base and WAL to the named pre-mistake target. 103 returns, 107 is absent, P3 is 10.</li><li>Compare the closed accepted history: purchase-edda-107 is valid excluded work, not part of the bad transaction.</li><li>Apply 107, its line and its stock decrement atomically with the request identity. P3 is 9. Repeating that identity adds nothing.</li><li>Accept database invariants and external-effect decisions, then transfer authority while the old source remains fenced.</li></ol></details>
 <p class="caption">Conceptual sequence matching the local drill. The final acceptance includes external authorities in a real service; this drill sends no payment, message or email. No incident duration is implied by spacing.</p>
</figure>
<style>
figure{font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-family:var(--font-serif)}

.restore{margin:2rem 0}.restore figcaption{font-size:1.12rem;margin-bottom:.8rem}.restore figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:.6rem}.history{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.history div{border-top:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .2rem}.history b,.history div span{display:block;font-size:.8rem}.history div span{color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.4rem}.states{display:grid;gap:.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.states>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:9rem 1fr;gap:1rem}.states b{font-size:.85rem}.states p{font-size:.9rem;margin:0;min-height:3rem}.restore>[data-explanation]{min-height:6rem;padding:.5rem .8rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent)}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.controls button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.4rem .7rem;cursor:pointer}.controls button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.controls [aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}[data-step]{margin-left:auto;align-self:center;font:.8rem var(--font-mono)}[data-hold]{height:3px;background:var(--color-rule);flex-basis:100%}[data-hold] span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin:.8rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:500px){.history{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:.7rem;gap:.2rem}.history>span{transform:rotate(90deg);justify-self:center}.history div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.5rem}.history div span{margin:0}.states{padding:.7rem}.states>div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.2rem}.restore>[data-explanation]{min-height:9rem}}
</style>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-r19-restore]').forEach(root=>{
 const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector(s) as HTMLElement;
 const scenes=[
 ['Open · still accepting requests','Not restored','No authority transfer','The bad transaction removed order 103. Valid order 107 then took P3 stock from 10 to 9.'],
 ['Fenced · all earlier work resolved','Not restored','Closed accepted history captured','The fence waits for previously admitted writers. A request racing behind it is rejected. Only now can the accepted history be enumerated without a moving boundary.'],
 ['Fenced','103 present · 107 absent · P3 stock 10','Database starts; business acceptance pending','The base and saved WAL reach the named target before the bad transaction. Both the mistake and later valid 107 are excluded.'],
 ['Fenced','103 present · 107 absent · P3 stock 10','One known valid request to reconcile','The frozen history contains purchase-edda-107 for Edda: one P3 at 4.50. Restoring to the right point did not put that later purchase back.'],
 ['Fenced','103 and 107 present · P3 stock 9','107 applied once; external checks pending','Create 107 and its line, decrement stock and record the request identity in one transaction. Repeating the same identity finds that outcome and leaves stock at 9.'],
 ['Remains fenced','Accepted candidate · P3 stock 9','Transfer only after every acceptance passes','Verify the restored rows, identities and stock, then settle the external-effect decisions. Transfer authority while the old source remains unable to accept writes.']
 ];
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>scenes.length,draw(s:number){const a=scenes[s];q('[data-source]').textContent=a[0];q('[data-candidate]').textContent=a[1];q('[data-accept]').textContent=a[2];q('[data-explanation]').textContent=a[3];}});
});
</script>
